1 शम् श॑मति शम्यति pp. शमित॑ labour, work;
 make
ready, prepare ((r.)). — Cf. शशमान॑.

2 सम॑ a. even, smooth, parallel;
 like, equal to (instr.,
gen., or —˚) or in (instr., तस्, loc., or —˚);
 (always) the same,
unaltered;
 common, mediocre;
 indifferent, neutral;
 harmless, good,
honest, fair, convenient, easy. n. & ˚— adv. equally, like, along,
together, precisely, exactly, fairly;
 n. as subst. plain, evenness,
balance, compensation, right measure or proportion, indifference,
equanimity.

स॑मन n. meeting, encounter, intercourse, assembly,
embrace;
 contest, fight.

समना॑ adv. in one point, together;
 at once,
simultaneously;
 equally, in like manner.

समा॑वन्त् a. equal, so great or so much (many);
 n. adv.
so much.

2 शमाय् शमा˚यति seek for peace of mind;
 ˚य॑ते bring
to rest i.e. kill.

शमीगर्भ॑ a. grown or resting in a Śamī-tree;
 m.
the holy fig-tree.

शमीसुमनस् f. Śamī-flower;
 ˚नोमाला f. garland of
Śamī-flowers.

शाम्बर॑ f. ई relating to Śambara;
 n. jugglery,
sorcery.

साम्य n. equality, resemblance or likeness to (instr.
±सह, gen., loc., or —˚);
 right or normal condition;
 equanimity,
impartiality, justice.

शामित्र a. relating to the slayer or cutter of the
sacrificial victim;
 m. the fire for cooking the sacrif. flesh;
 n. a
place for slaying cattle or = seq.

स॑मूल a. having roots, living, verdant;
 along with the
root, complete, entire, ˚— & n. adv.

समकक्ष a. of the same weight or importance;
 f. आ =
˚ता f., ˚त्व n. as abstr.

स॑मग्र f. समग्रा॑ whole, complete, full, entire, all;
n. everything;
 ˚— wholly.

सम॑ञ्जन a. fitting together;
 n. rubbing in,
anointing.

समनन्तर a. immediately adjoining, nearest to (abl.
or gen.);
 n. (& ˚—) immediately behind or after (abl., gen., or —˚).

सामन्त a. being all around, surrounding, neighbouring. m.
neighbour, vassal;
 n. neighbourhood.

सामान्य a. like, similar, common to or with (instr.
±सह or —˚);
 ordinary, vulgar;
 general, universal. n. equality,
congruence, right proportion, normal condition, totality, universality.
°—, instr., & abl. in general, generally, सामान्यम् adv. in common,
together;
 in the manner of, like (—˚).

स॑मन्यु (समन्यु॑) a. unanimous, harmonious;
 wrathful,
angry, dejected, sad.

समय॑ m. meeting or place of meeting, intercourse with
(instr.), agreement, convention, contract, obligation, condition;
 trial,
ordeal, (a fixed) point of time, i.g. time, season, occasion;
 case,
occurrence, circumstance;
 rule, norm, doctrine;
 custom, usage.

सम॑या (instr. adv.) in the middle of, betwixt (acc., r.
instr.);
 near, close to (acc., instr., or *gen.);
 half (˚—);
throughout, w. भू lie between.

समर्थ a. corresponding, suitable, fit for (gen. or
—˚);
 a match for (gen.);
 able to, capable of (infin., loc., dat., or
—˚);
 having the same sense or meaning (g.).

सामर्थ्य n. adequacy, fitness, sufficient cause for or
just claim on (loc. or —˚);
 strength, power, efficacy, ability (infin.,
dat., loc., or —˚);
 the meaning or function of a word. Abl. ˚योगात्
according to circumstances, by reason or on account of (—˚).

समवाय m. meeting with, joining (gen. or —˚);
congress, assembly;
 union, connection, mixture, aggregate;
 intimate
cohesion, inherence, adj. ˚यिन् (ph.).

समावृत्त a. returned (esp. from the teacher's house),
come back from (—˚);
 finished.

स॑मष्टि f. reaching, attaining;
 aggregate, totality,
abstr. ˚ता f.

समाकुल a. crowded, filled with, abundant in (instr. or
—˚);
 disturbed, perplexed, confused.

समागम m. coming together, meeting, union, intercourse
(also sexual) with (gen., instr. ±सह, or —˚);
 assembly, company.

समाधान n. placing, setting up (esp. the sacred fire),
arranging, settling, composing, making up, propitiating, reconciling;
attention, meditation, devotion.

समाधि m. putting together, conjunction, union, a whole;
performation, accomplishment, arrangement, reconcilement;
 attention,
meditation, devotion.

समाधेय a. to be put in order;
 to be directed or
instructed;
 to be conceded or admitted.

2 समानाधिकरण a. coordinate, having the same
government or subject with (instr. or —˚);
 abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

समानार्थ a. having the same purpose or meaning with
(instr. or —˚);
 abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

समानोदक a. distantly related (cf. सपिण्ड);
 abstr.
˚भाव m.

समानोदर्य a. born from the same womb;
 m. such a
brother.

समापत्ति f. meeting, encountering;
 incident, chance;
reaching, attaining, becoming (—˚).

समापन a. & n. accomplishing, performing;
 f. आ the
highest degree.

समाम्नात a. remembered, mentioned, enumerated;
 n.
mention, enumeration.

समायुत a. put or brought together;
 consisting of or
connected with (—˚).

समायोग m. junction, connection, contact with (instr.
±सह or —˚);
 arrangement, preparation;
 instr. by means or in
consequence of (—˚).

समारूढ a. mounted, entered (act. & pass.);
 grown,
increased;
 healed.

समाविष्ट a. seized or overcome by, filled or endowed
with (instr. or —˚);
 instructed in (instr.) by (instr.).

समाश्रय m. connection, junction with or relation to
(—˚);
 refuge, shelter, dwelling-place;
 adj. —˚ living or situated in,
relating or belonging to.

समाश्रित a. leaning or resting on, resorted to, entered
or being in (acc., loc., or —˚), got to, arrived at (acc.);
 devoted to,
intent upon (acc. or —˚);
 relating or belonging to (—˚);
 pass.
resorted to, sought, chosen;
 visited or afflicted by (instr. or —˚).

समासक्त a. attached to, fixed on (loc.);
 relating to,
occupied with (loc. or —˚).

समास्थित a. standing or sitting upon (acc., loc., or
—˚);
 remaining in (loc.);
 having incurred or got to (—˚).

समा॑हित a. put or fixed on, connected or linked with
(instr. or —˚);
 caused, produced, made, rendered;
 careful,
concentrated, intent upon (loc. or —˚);
 settled, proved, agreed;
finished, concluded.

स॑मिति f. meeting, assembly, union, league;
 encounter,
battle.

समि॑ध् a. flaming. — f. log of wood, fuel;
 kindling,
flaming.

समीकरण n. abstr. to seq. w. कृ;
 also
assimilation, digestion.

समी@कृ make even or equal to (instr.);
 ˚भू pass. or
refl.

समीक्षण a. causing to see, showing;
 n. looking at,
observing.

समीरण a. setting in motion, exciting;
 m. = prec., also
the god of the wind.

समुच्चय m. heap, mass, multitude, a whole or
aggregate;
 addition, copulative relation (g.).

समुत्थान n. rising, reviving, swelling, increasing;
activity, undertaking, beginning, enterprise (w. संभूय cooperation,
partnership);
 healing, cure.

समुत्थित a. risen, raised, high;
 sprung or produced
from (abl.), appeared, grown (wings);
 ready or prepared for (loc. or
infin.).

समुत्पन्न a. born, produced, begotten by (abl.) with
(loc.);
 come, arrived.

समुत्सुक a. agitated, uneasy, anxious, longing for
(infin. or —˚);
 abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

समुदाचार m. presenting, offering (—˚);
 good or
correct behaviour (p. ˚वन्त्);
 intercourse with (instr.).

†समुद्ग m. tip, point (only —˚);
 a small round box (also
˚क m.).

समुद्धर्तृ m. who lifts up or draws out;
 deliverer,
redeemer.

समुद्भव m. rising, origin, revival;
 adj. —˚ sprung
from.

समुद्भूत a. sprung up, produced, risen;
 being,
existing.

समुद्यम m. lifting up, raising;
 effort, exertion, zeal
for (loc., dat., or —˚).

सामुद्र a. oceanic, marine;
 m. mariner, sailor, pl. N. of
a people;
 n. sea-salt.

समुन्नत a. lifted up, risen;
 prominent, projecting;
high, sublime.

समुपस्थित a. come near, approached, come to (acc),
sitting or lying on (loc.);
 risen, appeared, arrived, fallen to one's
(acc. or gen.) share;
 imminent, future, ready for (acc. or gen.);
 fixed
upon, undertaken.

समुपेत a. met, assembled, arrived;
 connected or
provided with (instr.).

समूहन a. & n. sweeping together, collecting;
 f. ई
broom.

स॑मृद्ध a. achieved, perfect, complete;
 endowed with,
possessed of (instr., abl. or —˚);
 prosperous, wealthy, copious,
abundant.

समेत a. come to, got at (acc.);
 met, assembled;
 joined or
connected with, possessed of (instr. or —˚).

सम्य॑ञ्च् f. समीची॑ or समी॑ची turned to one point or
against each other, universus or adversus;
 whole, entire, all;
 correct,
right, true. n. सम्य॑क् adv. towards one point, together, truly,
correctly, exactly, duly, thoroughly;
 w. neg. not at all.

सम्रा॑ज् m. lord of the universe, sovereign ruler (f.
स॑म्राज्ञी);
 E. of Varuṇa, Indra, etc.

2 सा॑मन् n. song, esp. sacred song, a Vedic stanza arranged
for chanting;
 pl. the Sāmaveda.

सामासिक f. ई relating to a compound word;
 concise,
succinct, brief. m. n. a compound word.

सामिधेन॑ a. relating to fuel and kindling;
 f. ई॑
such a verse ((r.)).

सामुद्रक (a. = prec. a.*);
 f. ˚द्रिका a kind of leech;
n. sea-salt.
